values
  ('64b7ea7d-11e6-56ee-82d1-4421d0f8f048', '445534c6-3df0-5148-a006-78993ad8b6cd', 'Army', 'enlisted', '42A', 'Human Resources Specialist', 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal', 'Chapter 3. Recommended Career Management and Self-Development, By Rank', 'Soldiers should study, become familiar with, and understand military publications (can be found on the Army Publishing Directorate website at https://armypubs.army.mil/) related to equipment and duty skills associated with their MOS and assignment such as: STP 21–1–SMCT; ADP 6- 22; TC 3–21.5; TC 3–22.9; FM 7-22; FM 4-1; ATP 1-0.1; ATP 1-0.2; AR 25–50; AR 670–1; DA PAM 600-25; AR 600 series; all -10 level maintenance manuals associated with their equipment; and Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills (WTBD) associated with their current assignment. The following are suggested for self-development: TC 7–22.7 and http://www.train.army.mil/ contain additional reading material for self-development.
(1) Self-development competitive: Soldier boards, such as Soldier of the Quarter/Year broaden the knowledge base, instill discipline and improve the Soldier’s ability to communicate verbally.
(2) Data application: Microsoft 210/211
insert into public.reference_sources
