  ('92bfd0ce-5b4a-5a23-a80d-31609897ccb5', '445534c6-3df0-5148-a006-78993ad8b6cd', 'Army', 'enlisted', '42A', 'Human Resources Specialist', 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant', 'Chapter 3. Recommended Career Management and Self-Development, By Rank', '(1) The SSG’s professional competence is measured by how well they develop, maintain and use the full range of human potential of their Soldiers. This is typically the first level of leadership at which the NCO is responsible for leading and developing other leaders. SSGs should continue to hone leadership skills and maintain a high proficiency level in their MOS.
(2) SSGs will study and develop proficient knowledge of SL10 and SL20 publications in addition to the following military publications: STP 21–24–SMCT; DA PAM 611-21; DA PAM 600-25; ADP 1–02; ADP 3–90; AR 350–1; FM 4-1; all -10 level maintenance manuals associated with their equipment; and battle drills associated with their current assignment.
